<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Het Volk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1905–1911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Het Volk, 'The People', was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> political party founded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> in 1905 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-botha">Louis Botha</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-smuts">Jan Smuts</a> to work for self-government and reconciliation with English-speaking whites after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. It won the first elections of the self-governing Transvaal Colony in 1907, making Botha prime minister, and merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-party">South African Party</a> after union in 1910.</p></div>
